{
  "contract": "messaging",
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "description": "The conformance corpus for standards/055-messaging.md. Three parts. 'validity' is judged by envelope.schema.json alone. 'delivery' is judged by running a consumer: deliver the sequence in order and count the distinct effects an idempotent consumer produces (AM3); a delivery may carry 'fails' to model a handler failure followed by redelivery. 'signing' is judged by computing: given the secret, id, timestamp and exact body bytes, the webhook-signature value an implementation must produce, and deliveries it must reject (AM7, AM8). Signature values here were computed with HMAC-SHA256 over id + '.' + timestamp + '.' + body, keyed by the base64-decoded secret, per Standard Webhooks.",
